// Write-path policies: a card is prepared, confirmed by a "да", then executed.
//
// Cedar semantics: a request is denied unless a permit matches it, and a
// matching forbid beats every permit. The PDP keeps one history of requests
// per chat session, so the temporal rules see only that session's requests,
// allowed and denied alike.

// 1. Only a client with the write scope may prepare a card. The input must
// not name a subscriber: the subject comes from the token. The PDP checks
// only the policy against the schema, not the requests, so these checks are
// the only ones that refuse such a key.
permit (principal, action == Tel::Action::"Prepare", resource)
when {
    context.input.role == "client"
    && context.input.scopes.contains("tariffs:write")
    && !(context.input has user_id)
    && !(context.input has account)
    && !(context.input has subscriber)
    && !(context.input has msisdn)
};

// 2. A "да" confirms only a card prepared earlier in the session, with the
// same id, action and details: it can't confirm a card nobody was shown.
// The window never closes in the running PDP (its events carry no time), so
// the PDP checks the card's lifetime itself.
//
// POST-QA: let the policy check the card's lifetime. The PDP stamps its clock
// into every request (input.now, seconds) and a Prepare's deadline
// (input.expires_at = now + CARD_TTL_SEC); the schema gains both as Long.
// This rule binds the deadline the Prepare recorded and compares it, checked
// on dogwood-py 0.0.12:
//     exists (deadline: Long).
//         (formerly within 1h Tel::Action::"Prepare"::request{
//             ..., input.expires_at: deadline })
//         && deadline >= context.input.now
// Rule 3 gets the same check, or a refused late "да" in the history would
// open Execute. Then the clock check in PolicyService.confirm goes.
// `within 1h` stays: Dogwood requires a window after `formerly`. Not before
// QA: the course checks the windows with replays, and a replayed event
// without these fields would get Deny.
permit (principal, action == Tel::Action::"ConfirmCard", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Tel::Action::"Prepare"::request{
        input.pending_id: context.input.pending_id,
        input.action: context.input.action,
        input.details: context.input.details
    }
};

// 3. Only a confirmed card runs: the same card had a ConfirmCard before.
permit (principal, action == Tel::Action::"Execute", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Tel::Action::"ConfirmCard"::request{
        input.pending_id: context.input.pending_id,
        input.action: context.input.action,
        input.details: context.input.details
    }
};

// 4. At most two tariff changes per session. count_distinct_within counts
// distinct values of `card`, the pending_id: a repeated "да" or a retry of
// one card takes one slot. The current request counts too, so the third
// card is refused. The first condition keeps services and contacts out of
// the limit.
forbid (principal, action == Tel::Action::"Execute", resource)
when { context.input.action == "tariff_change" }
when temporal {
    count_distinct_within(card, 24h, Tel::Action::"Execute"::request{
        input.action: "tariff_change",
        input.pending_id: card
    }) > 2
};
